The scheme $L^\star $ is the $\mathbf{G}_ m$-torsor over $X$ associated to $L$. This is why the grading we get below is a $\mathbf{Z}$-grading, compare with Groupoids, Example <a href="/tag/0EKJ" data-tag="0EKJ">39.12.3</a> and Lemmas <a href="/tag/0EKK" data-tag="0EKK">39.12.4</a> and <a href="/tag/0EKL" data-tag="0EKL">39.12.5</a>.